traction rather than substitute a current leaderboard. The audit attributes CC0-1.0 to the MTEB results according to the task data specification; it also notes the absence of a standalone license file in the pinned archive. The Open LLM dataset license is undeclared. Public access is not permission to redistribute that table; reproduction should reacquire it rather than assume redistribution rights.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluation/audit.json#sources,extraction]]\n\nRepeated MTEB model/column measurements use the deterministic lexicographically first revision. Exact duplicate raw documents retain only the archive-first owner and other copies become missing before splitting. Full score-example hashes are computed before downstream preprocessing. The family heuristic combines namespace and a lowercased model stem before punctuation/digits; Open LLM uses the base-model metadata when available. Such deterministic bookkeeping is reproducible but cannot recover unrecorded lineage.\n\nThe documented evaluation environment is CPython 3.12.15 on Linux x86\\_64, NumPy 1.26.4, SciPy 1.12.0, and PyArrow 16.1.0. The benchmark evaluator requires native Landlock and seccomp isolation and a broker; a portable invocation on an unsupported kernel is not an equivalent reproduction. The exact entrypoint command is\n\\begin{samepage}\n\\begin{verbatim}\npython task/evaluate_final.py \\\n  --program_path \\\n  source_evidence/downstream/program/src/program.py \\\n  --results_dir /tmp/reproduced-final\n\\end{verbatim}\n\\end{samepage}\nThe command is documented for independent reproduction on a supported isolated host, not rerun during manuscript preparation; production used the broker-mediated interface. Seeds are fixed by the evaluator to $1009,1013,1019$. The retained seed records report approximately $24.08$, $22.89$, and $23.08$ seconds respectively, excluding independent source acquisition. These are machine-dependent durations, not a runtime guarantee. No end-to-end acquisition/storage or benchmark-inference runtime was measured for this paper.\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluation/plan.json#runtime]]\n% @evidence[[source_evidence/evaluation/requirements.txt]]\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes]]\n\nAll manuscript tables and quantitative figures are generated by \\path{build_paper_artifacts.py} directly from \\path{paper_data.json}; this only summarizes saved measurements. The conceptual overview is prepared separately from the manuscript specification. \\path{README.md} gives figure/table mappings and build commands. Derived artifacts have adjacent provenance sidecars and the manuscript has inline evidence links in LaTeX comments.\n\n\\subsection{Complete retained seed comparisons}\nTable~\\ref{tab:seeds} gives each primary source/split/seed comparison. The pooled weighting averages target errors within rows before averaging rows and checkpoints, then gives equal weight to seeds, the two split cases per source, and the two sources. The reset replay is omitted here and from primary aggregates. Table~\\ref{tab:controls} retains all actual/control pairs for the studied policy; control scores are not mixed into the primary leaderboard.\n\n\\begin{table}[h]\n\\centering\\footnotesize\n% @evidence[[paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes]]\n\\begin{tabular}{llrrrrrr}\\toprule Source & Split/seed & Var LF & Rand LF & Info R & Med R & Offset & Means \\\\ \\midrule\nMTEB & M/1009 & 0.9528 & 0.9412 & 0.9500 & 0.9369 & 0.9340 & 0.9147 \\\\\nMTEB & M/1013 & 0.9470 & 0.9326 & 0.9410 & 0.9316 & 0.9262 & 0.8996 \\\\\nMTEB & M/1019 & 0.9490 & 0.9373 & 0.9439 & 0.9318 & 0.9277 & 0.9132 \\\\\n\\addlinespace\nMTEB & F/1009 & 0.9488 & 0.9376 & 0.9443 & 0.9345 & 0.9199 & 0.9042 \\\\\nMTEB & F/1013 & 0.9369 & 0.9211 & 0.9283 & 0.9158 & 0.9178 & 0.8810 \\\\\nMTEB & F/1019 & 0.9469 & 0.9384 & 0.9457 & 0.9378 & 0.9323 & 0.9170 \\\\\n\\addlinespace\nOpen LLM & M/1009 & 0.9595 & 0.9375 & 0.9535 & 0.9331 & 0.9133 & 0.9063 \\\\\nOpen LLM & M/1013 & 0.9582 & 0.9370 & 0.9529 & 0.9321 & 0.9143 & 0.9055 \\\\\nOpen LLM & M/1019 & 0.9597 & 0.9376 & 0.9540 & 0.9336 & 0.9156 & 0.9075 \\\\\n\\addlinespace\nOpen LLM & F/1009 & 0.9619 & 0.9422 & 0.9579 & 0.9364 & 0.9182 & 0.9228 \\\\\nOpen LLM & F/1013 & 0.9594 & 0.9387 & 0.9539 & 0.9359 & 0.9168 & 0.9081 \\\\\nOpen LLM & F/1019 & 0.9531 & 0.9358 & 0.9533 & 0.9334 & 0.9111 & 0.9027 \\\\\n\\addlinespace\n\\bottomrule\\end{tabular}\n\\caption{All retained primary scores. M/F denotes model/name-family split; LF denotes low-rank reconstruction; R denotes ridge. Values are averages over the source-specific budget checkpoints, not single-budget scores.}\n{\n  \"scope\": \"Final evaluation results are independent of search selection. Implementation descriptions use the inspectable retained source, without claiming byte-identical final-snapshot identity.\",\n  \"claims\": [\n    {\"claim\": \"The final evaluation completed and qualified; qualification is not proof of broad generalization.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.qualification.status\", \"final.qualification.outcome\", \"final.qualification.correct\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"The retained original reference has zero measured search score change; three alternative evaluations are unscored and do not establish measured losses or failure causes.\", \"source_ids\": [\"study.selection_kind\", \"study.investigation_outcome\", \"study.search_score_delta\", \"study.attempts.total\", \"study.attempts.scored\", \"study.attempts.unscored\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"The pooled studied score is 0.9527636891 and equivalent normalized MAE is 0.0472363109; rounded values in the abstract, results, and pooled table are 0.9528 and 0.0472.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.combined_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Random-query low-rank pooled score is 0.9364101694, equivalent MAE 0.0635898306; the studied-minus-random difference is 0.0163535197.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.combined_score\", \"final.metric.random_lowrank_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"The supplied pooled paired family-clustered interval against random-query factors is [0.0148071678, 0.0184780194], not an interval against ridge or for subgroups.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_low\", \"final.metric.paired_gain_ci_high\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Information-selected ridge scores 0.9482262260 (MAE 0.0517737740), with descriptive studied-minus-ridge difference 0.0045374631 and no supplied paired significance interval.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.selected_ridge_score\", \"final.metric.combined_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Medoid ridge scores 0.9327472830 (MAE 0.0672527170), mean offset 0.9206056682 (MAE 0.0793943318), and historical means 0.9068768878 (MAE 0.0931231122).\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.medoid_ridge_score\", \"final.metric.copy_score\", \"final.metric.constant_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"The studied method has the highest pooled observed score among the six evaluated policies, without statistical superiority being established against all comparators.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.combined_score\", \"final.metric.random_lowrank_score\", \"final.metric.selected_ridge_score\", \"final.metric.medoid_ridge_score\", \"final.metric.copy_score\", \"final.metric.constant_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Three final seeds are 1009, 1013, 1019; replay is excluded from primary means and figures.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes\", \"source_evidence/evaluation/plan.json#aggregation\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Figure 2, supplementary Table 2, and derived_results.json retain each of the twelve primary source/split/seed cells and six policies, using control=false and replay=false.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"build_paper_artifacts.py\", \"derived_results.json\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"The studied policy has higher observed scores than random-query factors in all twelve retained primary cells and the highest three-seed mean in each of four source/split conditions.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"derived_results.json#conditions\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Studied condition means are 0.9496/0.9442 for MTEB model/family splits and 0.9591/0.9582 for Open LLM model/family splits, rounded from saved observations.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"derived_results.json#conditions\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Pooled source scores are 0.9468974985 for MTEB and 0.9586298797 for Open LLM; they do not constitute controlled source-difficulty comparisons.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.mteb_score\", \"final.metric.open_llm_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Open LLM family split at seed 1019 gives studied score 0.9531041725 versus information-selected ridge 0.9533160600, a retained local reversal.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\"], \"citation_keys\": [], \"evidence_refs\": [\"paper_data.json#final_evaluation.evaluation_evidence.episodes[2].solution.cases\"]},\n    {\"claim\": \"Pooled independently deranged-history score is 0.9233917542 and actual-minus-control gap is 0.0293719349.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.metric.permuted_score\", \"final.metric.corruption_gap\", \"final.metric.combined_score\"], \"citation_keys\": []},\n    {\"claim\": \"Every retained source/split/seed pair has a lower observed studied-policy score under historical-column derangement, as shown in Figure 3 and supplementary Table 3; the contrast changes learning, querying, and target composition jointly.\", \"source_ids\": [\"final.evidence.episodes\", \"final.met